<main id="main">

  <section id="about" aria-labelledby="about-h">
    <div class="row">
      <div class="head">
        <span class="label idx"><b>01</b> /</span>
        <h2 id="about-h">About</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="body about">
        <p>I design and run the foundations other engineers build on: architecture, infrastructure, identity and security, and the engineering standards that hold them together.</p>
        <p>Much of my recent work is about making AI-assisted delivery trustworthy. I hold agent-written code to the same standard as anyone's: a written spec before code, tests first, a hook that stops an agent finishing until typecheck, lint and tests pass, and adversarial review by a model from a second vendor.</p>
        <p>I do my best work where a small team needs to operate like a much larger one: setting technical direction through architecture decision records, choosing platforms on measured evidence, and automating the work nobody should do by hand.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

